---
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Find out about childcare sessions, funded places, Tax-Free Childcare, arranging a nursery tour, reserving a place and settling in at The Wonder Years Day Nursery." />
    <title>Fees, Funding and Joining the Nursery | The Wonder Years Day Nursery</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}styles/global.css`} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <div class="wireframe-banner">Fees, Funding and Joining wireframe · Content and image placement for review</div>
    <SiteHeader current="fees" />
    <main id="main">
      <section class="section hero">
        <div class="container hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">Fees and joining</p>
            <h1>Fees, Funding and Joining the Nursery</h1>
            <p class="lead">We understand that choosing childcare involves both practical decisions and finding somewhere that feels right for your child.</p>
            <p>This page explains the sessions available at The Wonder Years, the funded childcare options the nursery accepts and what happens when you are ready to arrange a visit and reserve a place.</p>
            <div class="button-row">
              <a class="button" href={`${base}contact/#enquiry`}>Arrange a nursery visit</a>
              <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Contact the nursery</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="image-placeholder hero-image" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a welcoming nursery arrival photograph">
            <span>Nursery arrival image placeholder</span>
            <small>Nursery entrance, reception area or a parent and child arriving for a visit</small>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-muted">
        <div class="container split-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Childcare sessions</p>
            <h2>Flexible options for families</h2>
            <p>The nursery offers flexible childcare to help meet the different needs of families.</p>
            <p>Available options include:</p>
            <ul><li>full-day care;</li><li>five-hour sessions; and</li><li>hourly childcare.</li></ul>
            <p>The team can talk through the available options with you during your nursery visit.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Tax-Free Childcare and childcare vouchers</p>
            <h2>Accepted payment support</h2>
            <p>The nursery accepts:</p>
            <ul><li>Tax-Free Childcare; and</li><li>childcare vouchers.</li></ul>
            <p>If you are unsure which funding or payment option applies to your family, the nursery team can explain what it accepts and where you may need to check your eligibility.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-accent">
        <div class="container">
          <p class="eyebrow">Funded childcare</p>
          <h2>Funded places from nine months</h2>
          <p>The Wonder Years offers funded childcare from nine months old for eligible families.</p>
          <p>This includes:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>funded childcare for eligible working families from nine months;</li>
            <li>Early Learning for Two;</li>
            <li>universal funded childcare for three- and four-year-olds; and</li>
            <li>up to 30 funded hours for eligible families.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Funded hours can be taken in different ways to help them work around family needs.</p>
          <p>The usual options are:</p>
          <ul><li>30 hours a week over 38 weeks of the year; or</li><li>22.5 hours a week over 50 weeks of the year.</li></ul>
          <p>Other patterns may also be considered, subject to the nursery’s available sessions.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container funding-panel">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">What is included</p>
            <h2>Food, drinks and activities</h2>
            <p>Food, drinks and nursery activities are included.</p>
            <p>Meals and snacks are prepared and cooked on the premises by the nursery cook, and allergies and dietary requirements are catered for.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Parents provide their child’s:</h3>
            <ul><li>nappies;</li><li>wipes;</li><li>creams; and</li><li>sunscreen, where these are needed.</li></ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-muted">
        <div class="container split-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Arranging a nursery visit</p>
            <h2>Come and explore the nursery</h2>
            <p>Prospective parents are encouraged to telephone or email to make an appointment for a nursery tour.</p>
            <p>A visit gives you the opportunity to:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>look around the nursery;</li><li>see the rooms and age groups;</li><li>meet members of the team;</li><li>discuss your child’s age, routines and needs;</li><li>talk about the sessions you are looking for;</li><li>ask about funded childcare; and</li><li>discuss current and expected availability.</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}contact/#enquiry`}>Arrange a nursery tour</a>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Reserving a place</p>
            <h2>Planning ahead</h2>
            <p>Once you have visited and decided that you would like your child to attend, the nursery can discuss reserving a place with you.</p>
            <p>The Wonder Years does not operate a traditional waiting list. Instead, places are booked using the nursery’s projected availability.</p>
            <p>Families are encouraged to visit and reserve their place as early as possible, as bookings are often made around 12 months in advance.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-accent">
        <div class="container split-grid reverse">
          <div class="image-placeholder landscape" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a welcoming nursery settling-in environment">
            <span>Settling-in image placeholder</span>
            <small>A calm nursery room, welcoming play area or staff member preparing an activity for a new child</small>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Settling in</p>
            <h2>Moving at your child’s pace</h2>
            <p>Every child responds differently to a new environment, so settling in is approached at the child’s own pace.</p>
            <p>The first settling-in visit usually lasts around 30 minutes. This gives your child time to meet the staff and begin becoming familiar with the room and nursery environment.</p>
            <p>Further visits are arranged after the team has met your child and seen how they respond. These sessions gradually build up to around two hours, with the aim of helping your child feel secure and comfortable before their usual childcare sessions begin.</p>
            <p>The nursery offers free settling-in visits to support this process.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container">
          <p class="eyebrow">What to discuss with the nursery</p>
          <h2>Information that helps the team</h2>
          <p>When you contact the team, it is helpful to share:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>your child’s age;</li><li>your preferred start date;</li><li>the days and hours you are looking for;</li><li>whether you may be eligible for funded childcare;</li><li>any dietary requirements or allergies; and</li><li>anything that may help the team understand your child’s routines or support needs.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>If there is anything specific you need to know about fees, funding, sessions or joining the nursery, please contact the team directly.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="final-cta">
        <div class="container">
          <h2>Ready to take the next step?</h2>
          <p>Come and visit The Wonder Years, meet the team and talk through the childcare you are looking for.</p>
          <div class="button-row centred">
            <a class="button button-light" href={`${base}contact/#enquiry`}>Arrange a nursery visit</a>
            <a class="button button-outline-light" href="tel:01215566979">Call 0121 556 6979</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer"><div class="container footer-grid"><div><strong>The Wonder Years Day Nursery Limited</strong><p>Company number: 08212428<br />Ofsted URN: 2710425</p></div><div><p>Arundel House, 50 Church Hill<br />Wednesbury, West Midlands, WS10 9DJ</p></div><nav aria-label="Footer navigation"><a href={`${base}contact/`}>Contact</a><a href={`${base}contact/#faqs`}>FAQs</a></nav></div></footer>
  </body>
</html>
